# Lesson 2, from the point-count exercise hand 9.
title: Two four-card suits: open the lower
id: L02-06
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.1, 2.2
student: S
board: 6
dealer: E
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  QT5    K97    Q4     J8643
  E  A63    T432   762    AQ5
  S  K842   AJ6    KJ95   72
  W  J97    Q85    AT83   KT9

auction:
  E Pass
  S 1D*    = 13+ points, at least four diamonds
     key: 12 HCP plus 1 for the doubleton club is 13: enough to open. With two four-card suits, open the lower-ranking one.
     not 1S: With two four-card suits, which one did the lesson say to open first?
     not Pass: Did you count 13? 12 HCP and the doubleton make an opening bid.
     not 1NT: 1NT shows 15-17. Did you count 12 HCP?
     not *: With two four-card suits, open the lower-ranking one.
  W Pass
  N 1NT    = 6-9 points, no four-card spades, not much diamond support
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = No game: at most 22
     key: Partner showed 6-9. Your 13 plus 9 is 22 at most, so stop.
     not 1S: 1NT says partner doesn't have four spades. Do you need to show yours?
     not 2NT: Did you add it up? 13 plus 6-9 can't reach 25.
     not 3NT: Did you add it up? 13 plus 6-9 can't reach 25.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  You opened the lower of your two four-card suits. Partner's 1NT showed
  6-9 points and no four-card spade suit (with one she'd have bid 1♠).
  Your side has at most 22, so you pass. North is declarer, because she
  bid no-trump first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E H2  S H6  W HQ  N HK
  2   N DQ  E D2  S D5  W DA
      note: Declarer's plan: set up tricks in diamonds, spades and hearts. First drive out the ♦A.
  3   W CK  N C3  E C5  S C2
      note: West switches to clubs.
  4   W CT  N C4  E CQ  S C7
  5   E H3  S HJ  W H5  N H7
  6   S S2  W S7  N ST  E S3
      note: Now a spade from dummy toward declarer's ♠Q and ♠T.
  7   N D4  E D6  S DK  W D3
      note: A diamond to dummy's king.
  8   S S4  W S9  N SQ  E SA
      note: Another spade, to drive out the ace.
  9   E H4  S HA  W H8  N H9
  10  S SK  W SJ  N S5  E S6
      note: Dummy's spades are winners now.
  11  S S8  W C9  N C6  E D7
      note: The last spade is high too.
  12  S DJ  W D8  N C8  E HT
      note: The ♦J.
  13  S D9  W DT  N CJ  E CA
      note: The ♦9 is a loser. 8 tricks: 1NT made with an overtrick.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: set up tricks in diamonds, spades and hearts, knowing
  the defenders will get chances to take their clubs.

  1NT made with an overtrick. Your side had 20 points, and the part score
  was the right place to stop.
